Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: aurora: enable Iris with OEM VPU33 firmware

Use the signed video firmware supplied by the board vendor. The stock and
upstream video memory regions both reserve 8 MiB at 0x9bb00000. Retain the
upstream SM8650 clocks, interconnects, IOMMU SIDs and HFI gen2 platform data.

Firmware provenance: pkgs/aurora/firmware/README.md

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-xiaomi-aurora.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-xiaomi-aurora.dts
@@ -316,3 +316,8 @@
 &usb_1_dwc3_hs {
 	remote-endpoint = <&pmic_glink_hs_in>;
 };
+
+&iris {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8650/xiaomi/aurora/vpu33_4v.mbn";
+	status = "okay";
+};
